 some superheroes for a while  and then ended up in a realm called  limbo now limbo exists in two forms of  marvel comics  there's the demonic realm of limbo then  there is the actual realm of limbo the  demonic realm of limbo is the one that's  ran by magic also known as ileana  rasputin you may or may not see that in  the mcu i honestly have no idea but the  actual realm of limbo is really what you  think of when you think of limbo right a  purgatory-like place  that exists outside of space and time  now for those of you guys who have been  doing some reading  outside of the loki tv show probably  doing it online or watching my videos or  comics explained or whatever you've  probably heard of a giant city called  chronopolis  and a castle of sorts in chronopolis  called tenebree that's the realm  of immortus the way this works is that  when rama tut traveled to limbo  he looked throughout the time stream and  saw that there were two possible futures  for himself the first is that he would  go back to his life as king  and the second is that he would become  an agent of the time keepers  and that in working for the time keepers  his job would be to ensure  that he essentially pruned the timeline  and made sure  that they came into existence he didn't  like the idea of working for the time  keepers  so he went back to being kang and then  kang went forward and did a whole bunch  of other stuff across marvel comics  but there is an alternate universe where  ramat stayed  in limbo and did become an agent of the  timekeepers and that guy became immortus  now immortus's role in marvel comics was  pretty simple  unlike king the conqueror who basically  traveled throughout the time stream  and faced off against various people  immortus largely just stayed in limbo  we'll talk about why that matters here  in a second he had a few interesting  stories here and there things like the  celestial madonna  the idea of avengers forever and so on  and so forth but overall the idea of  immortus was to look at the nature of  kang and to come to the realization  that kang was screwing up the time  stream so let's talk about kang for a  second  so if a mortise was a version of kang  who existed in limbo  and monitored what king prime as you can  call him was basically doing  then what kang prime was doing was  running throughout the different points  in the time stream  one of the things we covered in the  video that we did hear about the  multiverse explain in regards to marvel  comics here on gig culture explain  is we talked about the idea that  traveling into the past is not enough to  create an alternate reality in mobile  comics it's one of the big differences  between the comics and the mcu  just the very act of traveling into the  past or anywhere into the time stream  outside of where you're supposed to be  is enough to create a branch of universe  in the marvel cinematic universe so  there's kind of a big difference there  but in order to actually create an  alternate reality in marvel comics you  have to do a thing so kane the conqueror  could face off against the avengers and  then a whole  litany of alternate realities will  basically emerge based on  what possibilities could take place and  how that fight with the avengers could  go  and so because kane the conqueror had  done this on multiple occasions  throughout the history of the time  stream it led to him creating a ton of  alternate realities  and all these different alternate  realities basically had different  versions of kang  that had different scenarios about them  some of whom destroyed the avengers  some of whom got the infinity gauntlet  and destroyed the universe or  bent the universe to their whim some of  which conquered the entirety of their  universe but regardless of the situation  you had what was in effect  a council of kings now the kangs  themselves stretched on for a pretty  lengthy amount of time  and much like what you saw in the marvel  cinematic universe in the loki show  with the role of immortus which was  coming to this realization that all  these kings waging war against each  other essentially would have resulted in  the destruction of everything  that basically all the different kings  were defeated and mortis seemed to be  the last man standing  and in doing so created the tva as a  means to make sure  that no other branch universes would  emerge and that in ensuring that's the  case  no other kangs would pop up and so what  you have here is a situation  where jonathan majors is basically  immortus the issue is that jonathan  mages is now dead  he was killed by sylvie which means the  multiverse is now just kind of going  into full flux  and there's a few things that come out  of this right  the first and foremost let's talk about  what happened with  loki so loki himself was of course  pushed through the portal by sylvie  and ended up in this place where when he  went to meet with  mobius and b15 and kind of this  revelation of what was going on  they didn't remember who he was the  reason for that is because  loki's in an alternate reality and we  can deduce that he's in this alternate  reality for a couple different reasons  one we can say that he was inadvertently  pushed into an alternate universe by  sylvie  or we can say that when ravana rinslayer  basically went through her portal that  she ended up likely going into the past  and changing things regardless of how  you slice it loki's not in the same  universe now let's say that ravana  renaissance went into the past and she  altered things right she decided that  she wanted to work with kane the  conqueror  as opposed to working for kane the  conqueror and is basically fulfilling  her role as she exists in the comics  and really just kind of being a love  interest did you guys ever see the movie  deep impact where that giant meteor  crashed into the ocean and said this  giant tidal wave  just careening in virtually every  direction that's how changes in the time  stream work in this instance  ravana rinse layer is potentially the  asteroid hitting the water  and the changes to the time stream or  the tidal wave moving towards its final  destination  that's how this sort of thing works it's  a cascading effect  and so if ravana rensselaer went into  the past and she decided to work with  kang  once the multiverse was restored and  then in turn made it easier for  a particular version of king to become  this kind of person that basically found  the tva  instead of a mortise basically they won  the multiverse award then suddenly  everything shifts and everything changes  that while the events more or less  transpire the same throughout the  history of the loki show it's kane the  conqueror that you see as the statue at  the end of the show  instead of just a random time keeper the  entire timeline has shifted now let's  say for example that what's actually  going on here  is that loki was pushed into an  alternate reality by  sylvie how would this play out how would  it explain everything well one  it makes things a lot easier one of the  things to understand when it comes to  alternate realities in mobile comics and  by extension  at least to a degree the marvel  cinematic universe is that everything in  that universe  before that point where it branches off  stays the same  so say for example that you had an  alternate reality where peter parker  never became spider-man  everything up to that point in that  universe is still the same  it's just at that critical moment when  peter was supposed to be bitten by a  radioactive spider he went to the  bathroom instead and was never bitten by  that spider and then never became  spider-man instead maybe it was somebody  like wouldn't stacy or  or flash thompson or something along  those lines who really knows who really  cares but everything up to that point  is still the exact same and so if sylvie  pushed loki back to a point  where he basically ended up in an  alternate universe it's easy to slide  between one and the other  if you have something like a portal  maybe it's just one of these things  where he was kind of  shoved in that direction and that's  basically it we don't definitively know  it's just one of these things where it  just kind of seems to have branched off  one of the things to keep in mind is  that if you're in one of these finer  little nexus points  it's easy for you to just kind of slide  into an alternate reality  without being able to keep yourself in  the main universe but there's all kinds  of possibilities here how the marvel  cinematic universe  treats time travel is in a lot of ways  different from how marvel comics handles  it  makes a lot more sense which is  certainly a much much better thing but  at the end of the day the loki's show  was amazing like it was absolutely  awesome here's one of the funny things  though one of the big issues that a lot  of people are struggling with is  when loki takes place it's very very  easy for us to look at the loki tv show  and see that it comes after events like  avengers end game and infinity war  in terms of when marvel created it but  just because of the fact that the movie  was released after infinity war does not  mean it takes place  after the events of infinity war that  the tva exists in null space right  there's no time there  and so to impact the multiverse means to  impact the entire timeline  and so look at one division for a second  the post-credits scene  the idea that wanda basically heard the  voices of her kids and then took off  after it to basically find out what was  going on  it's entirely possible that her hearing  that coincides with the creation of the  multiverse and that once the multiverse  was formed there's now an alternate  reality out there where she was where  her kids basically survived  and that if we know somebody like  schumachorath and doctor strange 2 is  going to be a major villain  and schumacherath is aware of that and  given the history of his character that  he's aware of like nexus beings like  juan  maximoff it wouldn't be that hard if he  exists in the multiversal space  to reach out to wanda and trick her into  believing that her kids are alive but in  danger  and she has to go save them and then  capture her right these are the kind of  possibilities that can come  out of the loki tv show these are the  kind of things that you could be seeing  i don't know if we definitively will but  it is an awesome concept  regardless at the end of the day the  loki show was amazing i absolutely loved  it it was a fantastic show i had a great  time watching it  and i am very very very excited for  season two but with that being said guys  we're gonna bring this to an end  thank you guys for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace
 

